# 036 - the four escapes of §2 and what they do to the OBSERVABLE. `print
# "a\nb";` appends ONE element to Output.lines whose bytes contain a newline
# (§3: a Str displays as its bytes), which is exactly why §5 compares bytes and
# never splits lines: split-and-compare fails a CORRECT engine here.
--- source
print "a\nb";
print "x\ty";
print "q\\z";
print "he said \"hi\"";
--- expect
a
b
x	y
q\z
he said "hi"
